      "title": "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "034b7005-ba3b-5dbf-a095-a2b2dfa38ba3",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find $(2\\mathbf{f}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}$, where $t>0$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t)&=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{t} \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t)&=\\begin{bmatrix}- t \\\\ - t^{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Apply the **sum and constant multiple rules**:\n\n$$\n(2\\mathbf{f}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}=2\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)+\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t).\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{t}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ - 4 t^{3} \\\\ - \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nScale every component by its constant multiplier:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 1\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ - 4 t^{3} \\\\ - \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd corresponding components and combine like terms:\n\n$$\n(2\\mathbf{f}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}} \\\\ - 4 t^{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{t} - \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "adc6f92b-bec9-5445-b474-2984cbf38bd3",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
