    "question": {
      ":question/id": "99212dbc-cc08-50c8-9339-55c7cef7a51d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find $(-2\\mathbf{f}(t)-2\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}$, where $t\\in\\mathbb R$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t)&=- 6 \\mathbf{i} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\mathbf{j} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\mathbf{k} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t)&=2 \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 5 \\mathbf{j} - 4 \\mathbf{k} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Apply the **sum and constant multiple rules**:\n\n$$\n(-2\\mathbf{f}(t)-2\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}=-2\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)-2\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t).\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)&=6 \\mathbf{i} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\mathbf{j} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\mathbf{k} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\mathbf{j} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\mathbf{k} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nScale every component by its constant multiplier:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)&=- 12 \\mathbf{i} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\mathbf{j} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 12 \\mathbf{k} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ -2\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)&=- 2 \\mathbf{j} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 8 \\mathbf{k} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd corresponding components and combine like terms:\n\n$$\n(-2\\mathbf{f}(t)-2\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}=- 12 \\mathbf{i} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\mathbf{j} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 20 \\mathbf{k} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nKeep the displayed inner arguments when applying the scalar derivative rules; any nonunit inner derivative multiplies its component.",
