    "question": {
      ":question/id": "28faa91e-9592-5677-937f-7f858dd9bc17",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find $(\\mathbf{f}(t)+3\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}$, where $t\\in\\mathbb R$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t)&=\\langle 1 - 3 t,\\,2 t - 12,\\,14 t\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t)&=\\langle - 2 t^{2},\\,1 - t^{2},\\,t\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Apply the **sum and constant multiple rules**:\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{f}(t)+3\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}=\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)+3\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t).\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle -3,\\,2,\\,14\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle - 4 t,\\,- 2 t,\\,1\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nScale every component by its constant multiplier:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle -3,\\,2,\\,14\\rangle \\\\ 3\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle - 12 t,\\,- 6 t,\\,3\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd corresponding components and combine like terms:\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{f}(t)+3\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}=\\langle - 12 t - 3,\\,2 - 6 t,\\,17\\rangle.\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
